<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n70640" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νήϊστος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">η</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, 
			Sup.
		, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νήατος</span>
			 (v. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νέατος</span> A), in form
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νήϊστα: ἔσχατα, κατώτατα,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>: hence perh. the name of the <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πύλαι
				Νήϊσται</span> at Thebes, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πύλαισι
				Νηΐστῃσι</span> (
				v.l.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νηΐτῃσι [-τισι, -ταισι]</span>
			) <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Th.</u>
				460
			</span></i>, cf. Stat. <i><span class="en">
				<u>Theb.</u>
				8.354
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Νηΐταις πύλαις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Ph.</u>
					1104
				</span></i>
			 codd. (
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νήϊϊ, ταῖς πύλαις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hsch.
				</span></i>
			: perh. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Νηΐτταις πύλαις</span>
			with <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ττ</span>- from <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-στ</span>-).</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
